WEBVTT

00:06.027 --> 00:11.407
My calculations indicate we'll reach
the target in three minutes, 40 seconds.

00:12.067 --> 00:15.307
And when we get there, we'll have to deal
 with the Assassin and her agent?

00:17.227 --> 00:20.377
Hey, where's your musket?

00:20.807 --> 00:23.007
I gave it to an acquaintance.

00:23.517 --> 00:27.157
It looked like they really wanted it,
 and I figured I may as well.

00:27.157 --> 00:28.987
You shouldn't be so careless with it!

00:28.987 --> 00:31.537
That belonged to Siesta, you know!

00:32.437 --> 00:36.237
But... do you have a plan 
for how we win without a gun?

00:36.237 --> 00:38.787
Hmm? Not really.

00:38.787 --> 00:39.777
You don't?

00:40.157 --> 00:41.087
But...

00:42.027 --> 00:45.527
You have a plan, don't you?

00:50.457 --> 00:53.287
You're not going to tell me, are you?

00:54.437 --> 00:55.597
There they are.

00:58.047 --> 00:59.457
Let's go.

01:04.007 --> 01:07.557
EPISODE 5:
THAT WAS THEIR FINAL ANSWER

01:12.407 --> 01:14.107
Kimizuka?

01:14.417 --> 01:18.317
What? That robot is still functional?

01:20.067 --> 01:20.807
Do it.

01:28.707 --> 01:30.107
They want a fight.

01:30.447 --> 01:32.957
Initiating punishment.

01:40.617 --> 01:41.967
That's going too far!

01:42.277 --> 01:46.207
The Sirius Version Beta 
comes equipped with serious firepower.

01:46.207 --> 01:50.467
I know they got you once, 
but that's a brutal way to get revenge.

02:02.497 --> 02:03.607
I'll handle her.

02:04.047 --> 02:06.117
Get back, Kimihiko.

02:08.577 --> 02:11.287
Between you and that vampire...

02:11.927 --> 02:14.097
None of this was in the plan!

02:14.417 --> 02:16.187
The plan?

02:16.187 --> 02:18.677
I don't think that's the right way 
to think about this.

02:18.677 --> 02:21.667
What? You're lecturing me?

02:21.667 --> 02:25.427
No. I don't have the right to do that.

02:25.817 --> 02:32.127
But Siesta-sama wouldn't have blamed 
others for any failures in her own plan.

02:36.347 --> 02:40.437
Getting overly emotional 
is a bad habit of yours.

02:43.707 --> 02:45.627
Ma'am was the same way.

02:47.007 --> 02:50.077
I first met her five years ago.

02:50.637 --> 02:55.547
A certain organization 
ordered me to assassinate her.

03:05.457 --> 03:07.377
Oh, fine!

03:07.377 --> 03:10.177
Just kill me or whatever!

03:10.897 --> 03:15.577
I failed to assassinate you, 
so now they're going to kill me anyway!

03:15.577 --> 03:17.837
I just told you.

03:17.837 --> 03:20.427
Tell everyone I died here.

03:20.427 --> 03:23.147
Then they won't kill you.

03:24.537 --> 03:28.197
Why would you want me to do that?

03:31.867 --> 03:34.197
Why are you doing a job like this?

03:36.087 --> 03:38.207
Because of my parents.

03:38.707 --> 03:42.667
They were soldiers and spies.

03:43.267 --> 03:47.047
They protected this world 
from the shadows.

03:47.437 --> 03:52.407
So I'm proud of them... and of this job.

03:53.137 --> 03:54.427
I see.

03:54.427 --> 03:56.227
Same as me, then.

03:57.037 --> 04:00.557
I'm doing this job for my own reasons.

04:00.557 --> 04:04.447
So I can't let you kill me here.

04:06.637 --> 04:11.107
But if you're the same as me, 
you can't die here.

04:11.107 --> 04:13.547
So you'll help me?

04:13.547 --> 04:14.487
Yes.

04:14.877 --> 04:18.537
And I want you to help me
after this is over.

04:20.457 --> 04:22.327
That's the deal I'm offering.

04:23.037 --> 04:25.807
I'll save your life this time.

04:26.267 --> 04:31.087
And in exchange, 
help me out once in a while.

04:32.717 --> 04:35.307
I tried to kill you.

04:35.307 --> 04:38.097
You're asking me to help you?

04:38.947 --> 04:40.097
How about it?

04:41.617 --> 04:44.607
I knew instinctively...

04:45.447 --> 04:49.497
she didn't actually need my help.

04:49.957 --> 04:56.047
She was just saying it so it would be 
easier for me to let her help me.

04:57.977 --> 04:59.367
That's not fair...

05:03.467 --> 05:07.517
So, what should I do?

05:12.887 --> 05:18.027
And she gave me this pendant 
as proof of our deal.

05:18.787 --> 05:22.857
She always protected me.

05:22.857 --> 05:26.397
If I was helping the Tuners, 
that organization couldn't hurt me.

05:26.877 --> 05:29.077
She even set it up

05:29.077 --> 05:33.797
so that after her death, I could go work
 for another Tuner immediately.

05:33.797 --> 05:35.817
And that was Kase Fuubi?

05:36.597 --> 05:38.157
And even now...

05:38.157 --> 05:40.657
Even in that form...

05:40.657 --> 05:45.167
She's still going easy on me 
so she won't kill me!

05:45.167 --> 05:46.677
Why?!

05:47.117 --> 05:48.667
Why do you go easy on me?

05:48.667 --> 05:51.167
Why don't you take me seriously?

05:51.167 --> 05:54.927
Why are you still trying to protect me?

05:55.457 --> 05:58.467
A year ago, I couldn't do anything.

05:58.787 --> 06:00.407
So I swore...

06:00.407 --> 06:04.237
No matter what happened 
when I worked for that woman,

06:04.237 --> 06:09.527
I'd defeat SPES in her place!

06:09.977 --> 06:11.357
But you...

06:18.987 --> 06:22.617
I'll do anything to win!

06:26.757 --> 06:29.997
I knew you'd do that.

06:30.287 --> 06:31.467
It's over.

06:32.257 --> 06:33.567
Wait, Char!

06:34.257 --> 06:37.177
Can you really pull that trigger?

06:37.507 --> 06:39.317
What do you mean?

06:39.317 --> 06:41.647
Do you think I'd really hesitate?

06:41.647 --> 06:45.387
Even if that's the real Siesta's body?

06:48.197 --> 06:52.067
It's really her?

06:53.557 --> 06:55.127
You knew?

06:56.027 --> 06:59.197
When did you figure it out, Kimihiko?

06:59.567 --> 07:01.367
I'm not sure.

07:01.997 --> 07:06.417
I don't think it was any one thing.

07:07.777 --> 07:14.757
Siesta-sama's body was preserved
after the battle a year ago.

07:15.657 --> 07:20.397
And it was equipped 
with an artificial heart

07:20.397 --> 07:24.477
and an artificial intelligence
 with her memories.

07:24.477 --> 07:26.437
Thus, I was born.

07:28.117 --> 07:32.687
I thought that might be the case...

07:33.167 --> 07:36.607
I remember her scent, after all.

07:37.697 --> 07:39.697
But so what?

07:40.227 --> 07:46.017
Even if that's her body... 
my job doesn't change!

07:46.707 --> 07:51.277
Char! What Siesta left behind 
was the four of us!

07:51.277 --> 07:53.457
If you're going to carry on with her duty,

07:53.777 --> 07:56.327
none of us can die!

07:57.187 --> 07:59.717
But she was a Tuner!

07:59.717 --> 08:02.647
Her duty was to defeat SPES!

08:03.217 --> 08:05.927
Char! The teacher that you loved...

08:05.927 --> 08:10.297
Would she have chosen her duty
or her comrades?

08:11.127 --> 08:12.227
Shut up!

08:22.837 --> 08:24.237
Why...

08:24.537 --> 08:28.457
Why is she smiling so happily?

08:28.457 --> 08:29.457
This...

08:30.207 --> 08:31.457
This thing!

08:40.837 --> 08:42.087
That hurt.

08:42.917 --> 08:45.047
I'm... sorry...

08:52.567 --> 08:53.857
Why?

08:54.457 --> 08:55.777
Sheesh...

08:57.047 --> 08:59.507
Are you stupid?

09:01.707 --> 09:03.277
That's...

09:05.997 --> 09:08.887
That's the first time...

09:10.617 --> 09:13.967
you've ever said that to me...

09:19.207 --> 09:20.577
Ma'am...

09:26.497 --> 09:27.787
Noches!

09:31.747 --> 09:32.817
Ma'am!

09:34.507 --> 09:39.227
That's why I called you naive, Charlotte.

09:40.107 --> 09:43.187
I thought you were smarter than this.

09:43.677 --> 09:46.197
But you're no different than that kid.

09:47.267 --> 09:48.297
Noches!

09:48.697 --> 09:50.117
I'm fine.

09:50.787 --> 09:56.287
Damage this minor can be dealt with 
by activating my emergency shutdown.

09:56.287 --> 09:57.567
But...

09:57.567 --> 10:03.297
Your priority is to deal with her!

10:07.797 --> 10:09.707
I'll be right back.

10:18.557 --> 10:20.067
What's with you two?

10:20.067 --> 10:24.107
You were just pretending to be enemies, 
and now you're working together?

10:25.007 --> 10:28.827
You're sure about 
going against her, right?

10:29.127 --> 10:31.007
You'll lose a lot if you do.

10:34.817 --> 10:36.327
It's too late to care.

10:37.487 --> 10:38.837
First we'll attack from both sides!

10:42.517 --> 10:43.567
Too slow.

10:50.347 --> 10:51.967
That's one down.

11:02.397 --> 11:03.797
What will you do?

11:03.797 --> 11:05.647
It's just you now.

11:06.177 --> 11:09.517
Are you going to keep 
resisting for no reason?

11:09.517 --> 11:11.907
Don't you care what happens to the world?

11:12.357 --> 11:14.917
Of course I do!

11:15.417 --> 11:23.167
But she wouldn't want me 
to sacrifice someone to save the world!

11:23.417 --> 11:24.657
Yeah?

11:24.657 --> 11:28.607
Didn't the one who was sacrificed 
to save the world say it herself?

11:29.107 --> 11:32.757
That you were the last thing 
she left behind?

11:32.757 --> 11:34.797
Do you know what that means?

11:36.517 --> 11:40.037
It means that you are to carry on 
the work of the Great Detective

11:40.037 --> 11:42.767
and die for the sake of the world.

11:44.277 --> 11:45.917
I'll be honest.

11:46.527 --> 11:48.877
Natsunagi Nagisa isn't good enough.

11:48.877 --> 11:50.527
She's too weak.

11:51.097 --> 11:52.527
So Charlotte,

11:53.027 --> 11:57.307
you must carry on her will and become 
the new Great Detective as a Tuner.

11:58.397 --> 11:59.917
You always looked up to her, right?

12:02.647 --> 12:03.857
No...

12:05.397 --> 12:09.797
I didn't just look up 
to the Great Detective!

12:10.317 --> 12:11.997
I...

12:13.337 --> 12:18.047
I looked up to the strong, 
beautiful girl named Siesta!

12:19.667 --> 12:21.347
How boring.

12:26.787 --> 12:28.447
You underestimate me.

12:37.997 --> 12:40.787
Did you think you could 
beat me one-on-one?

12:43.537 --> 12:45.227
Playtime's over.

12:47.377 --> 12:48.377
Now!

12:53.967 --> 12:56.637
Nice hit, Nagisa-san!

12:56.637 --> 12:59.017
Siesta's seven tools are amazing.

12:59.377 --> 13:01.517
There was no recoil at all.

13:02.807 --> 13:05.517
She came back herself?

13:06.027 --> 13:07.047
Why?

13:07.527 --> 13:10.777
You're going to take her side?

13:10.777 --> 13:14.197
She tried to kill you!

13:15.787 --> 13:18.367
Yes! She's our comrade!

13:19.147 --> 13:22.537
And after that, we're gonna 
have a huge fight over it!

13:22.947 --> 13:25.507
That's okay, right, Char-san?

13:25.507 --> 13:27.967
She's not alone, you know.

13:27.967 --> 13:32.007
Yui-chan and I are gonna kill you twice!

13:32.757 --> 13:35.297
Yui... Nagisa...

13:35.637 --> 13:38.337
Don't worry. That won't happen.

13:39.687 --> 13:43.207
You're ready to die, right, Saikawa Yui?

13:43.557 --> 13:46.287
And Natsunagi Nagisa.

13:46.817 --> 13:48.317
Of course.

13:48.317 --> 13:51.817
Sorry, but I'm not gonna fire
 any warning shots.

13:59.827 --> 14:00.837
To the right!

14:05.597 --> 14:07.287
I knew I'd have to take you out first.

14:36.487 --> 14:38.237
Yui! Nagisa!

14:56.677 --> 14:59.757
You're still pretending to be friends?

15:00.177 --> 15:01.517
How stupid.

15:03.137 --> 15:05.137
It's not stupid!

15:05.457 --> 15:08.897
We're the last hope Siesta left behind!

15:08.897 --> 15:12.397
None of us will lose! 
None of us will give up!

15:12.397 --> 15:14.167
We'll all win together!

15:16.037 --> 15:17.857
What's with you people?

15:18.437 --> 15:23.447
Comrades, bonds, 
friendship, feelings, will...

15:23.957 --> 15:26.667
What good are they to the world?

15:26.987 --> 15:28.467
Saikawa Yui.

15:28.467 --> 15:31.167
If you die, the world will be saved.

15:31.167 --> 15:33.677
Charlotte Arisaka Anderson.

15:33.677 --> 15:37.047
If you kill Saikawa Yui,
the world will be saved.

15:37.547 --> 15:39.477
Natsunagi Nagisa.

15:39.477 --> 15:44.207
If you could be as strong as the last
Great Detective, the world would be saved!

15:44.957 --> 15:47.297
Why don't any of you do it?

15:47.297 --> 15:48.347
You can't?

15:48.797 --> 15:51.097
I see. You can't, huh?

15:51.797 --> 15:56.607
Then you should at least 
be ashamed of that...

15:57.467 --> 16:01.047
And not get in the way of the people 
who <i>are</i> fighting to save the world!

16:02.807 --> 16:04.087
You're right.

16:04.637 --> 16:07.707
I don't think what you're saying is wrong.

16:08.117 --> 16:11.077
Some people would say what 
you're doing is the right thing.

16:11.527 --> 16:15.337
But the detective 
who was always right is dead.

16:16.287 --> 16:21.867
So I want to make a choice 
that might be wrong!

16:22.537 --> 16:24.287
I want to choose a future

16:24.287 --> 16:28.097
where the people I care about 
are smiling with me when it's over!

16:28.347 --> 16:32.257
I don't want to let anyone else die!

16:34.497 --> 16:36.027
This is a waste of time.

16:37.217 --> 16:39.717
Then that makes it easy.

16:40.447 --> 16:43.077
The one still standing 
at the end is the winner.

16:43.867 --> 16:45.867
You're evil and must be destroyed.

16:49.367 --> 16:50.397
Nagisa!

16:50.397 --> 16:51.487
Don't worry.

16:51.997 --> 16:57.307
I can't see her, but she's looking at me.

16:57.307 --> 16:59.507
Hearing my voice.

16:59.507 --> 17:03.027
So this power is sure to activate.

17:04.107 --> 17:05.327
Kase Fuubi.

17:06.157 --> 17:09.137
You're frozen in place.

17:16.227 --> 17:21.177
Don't think you can stop me 
with some cheap new power!

17:22.997 --> 17:27.727
You think the three of you 
can really stop me?

17:29.527 --> 17:30.767
Wait...

17:31.937 --> 17:33.117
Three?

17:34.087 --> 17:36.037
That robot is out of commission.

17:36.657 --> 17:41.547
Since when have I been fighting
 the three of them?

17:42.247 --> 17:44.497
Hey, where is he?

17:44.497 --> 17:46.917
Where is Kimizuka Kimihiko?

17:49.887 --> 17:52.597
You made the right call.

17:53.187 --> 17:56.827
Your priority was taking down 
Char and the others.

17:57.817 --> 18:02.327
You could've easily dealt 
with anything I might've tried.

18:03.597 --> 18:06.967
But you made one mistake.

18:07.747 --> 18:09.887
Kimizuka Kimihiko...

18:09.887 --> 18:13.557
You swallowed Chameleon's seed!

18:16.227 --> 18:17.877
Side effects?

18:17.877 --> 18:19.457
I don't give a shit.

18:20.767 --> 18:23.497
<i>I'm sure she'd get mad...</i>

18:24.777 --> 18:29.177
<i>But for now, all I care about is punching
this dipshit detective in the face.</i>

18:29.787 --> 18:33.517
<i>She's taken the justice 
my partner loved and perverted it...</i>

18:33.517 --> 18:36.647
<i>And all I want to do is punch her!</i>

18:37.597 --> 18:39.647
Is that what you really want?

18:43.387 --> 18:44.477
Sure.

18:45.087 --> 18:47.777
I'm not causing trouble for anybody.

18:49.527 --> 18:51.187
Am I?

18:52.287 --> 18:53.657
<i>This is...</i>

18:57.267 --> 18:59.137
<i>my story!</i>

19:08.477 --> 19:11.567
You're a bold man, 
arresting a police officer.

19:12.597 --> 19:16.997
I still can't believe 
you swallowed the seed, though.

19:16.997 --> 19:17.847
Yeah.

19:18.737 --> 19:20.937
It was a gift from the vampire.

19:22.387 --> 19:24.607
You're going to die.

19:26.747 --> 19:29.117
Well, I'll deal with that when it happens.

19:30.337 --> 19:31.947
I see.

19:31.947 --> 19:35.127
All right, go join them then.

19:37.797 --> 19:39.177
Ma'am...

19:39.787 --> 19:41.127
Listen to me...

19:41.537 --> 19:45.627
I'm not her... Charlotte...

19:45.627 --> 19:46.907
Noches-san!

19:46.907 --> 19:48.127
Are you okay?

19:49.747 --> 19:52.607
You always make far too much noise...

19:53.517 --> 19:57.017
I won't be able to take a nap.

19:57.017 --> 19:59.767
Noches, are you okay?

20:01.517 --> 20:04.717
I've more than done my duty.

20:05.377 --> 20:07.277
What do you mean?

20:07.907 --> 20:12.407
Each of you had something 
you needed to overcome.

20:13.177 --> 20:17.137
I am just a program 
created to help you with that.

20:17.927 --> 20:22.447
Natsunagi Nagisa had to learn 
who she really was

20:22.447 --> 20:24.877
and face her own past.

20:25.657 --> 20:29.527
Saikawa Yui had to accept 
the truth of her parents' deaths

20:29.527 --> 20:32.227
and choose what she'd do with her life.

20:33.007 --> 20:38.107
Charlotte Arisaka Anderson 
had to be released from her duty

20:38.107 --> 20:41.107
and gain a will of her own.

20:41.987 --> 20:48.467
And Kimizuka Kimihiko needed to move on
 from Siesta-sama's death.

20:50.057 --> 20:52.687
I've done my job.

20:52.687 --> 20:57.597
Now Siesta-sama 
can move on without regrets.

21:01.287 --> 21:03.057
Is that really true?

21:04.107 --> 21:10.587
Even if we've moved on from the past 
and the things that bind us,

21:10.977 --> 21:13.587
does that really mean 
she had a happy ending?

21:14.477 --> 21:15.757
Kimihiko...

21:16.597 --> 21:19.247
She was crying...

21:19.677 --> 21:22.967
She was crying 
and saying she didn't want to die.

21:24.497 --> 21:28.207
If this was really what she wanted,

21:28.907 --> 21:31.807
she wouldn't have let us 
see her crying like that!

21:32.197 --> 21:38.197
Noches, didn't you decide 
to show us that part on your own?

21:38.197 --> 21:43.957
You wanted us to fix the mistake 
Siesta made when she sacrificed herself!

21:44.277 --> 21:48.027
That was the real answer 
you wanted us to find!

21:55.397 --> 21:57.957
Kimihiko, what are you...

21:58.307 --> 22:00.057
Listen to me, Siesta.

22:01.657 --> 22:03.667
I won't give up on you!

22:04.437 --> 22:07.467
Even if you're satisfied with this ending,

22:08.297 --> 22:10.497
I'll never accept it!

22:11.557 --> 22:15.267
Maybe nobody will understand it.

22:15.267 --> 22:18.447
Not Natsunagi, nor Saikawa, nor Charlotte!

22:19.217 --> 22:23.797
And maybe it is going 
against the laws of this world!

22:24.207 --> 22:29.477
But someday, I'll bring you back!

22:29.477 --> 22:32.107
I promise... I promise I will!

22:38.847 --> 22:41.217
You're an idiot, Kimizuka.

22:43.327 --> 22:45.977
You're an idiot.

22:46.547 --> 22:50.567
You're an idiot, Kimizuka.

22:54.447 --> 22:55.667
Sheesh...

22:58.517 --> 23:01.127
Are you all stupid?

23:09.287 --> 23:11.427
The sun's up.

23:12.257 --> 23:13.497
Yeah.

23:13.497 --> 23:14.687
This is where it begins.

23:16.117 --> 23:18.927
<i>The detective is already dead?</i>

23:21.327 --> 23:22.277
<i>No...</i>

23:22.657 --> 23:26.737
<i>This is the long, long story...</i>

23:27.267 --> 23:31.487
<i>of how I bring her back!</i>

23:34.987 --> 23:39.987
EPISODE 6:
GUARDIAN OF THE WORLD
